      "parent_index": null,
      "last_updated": "2026-05-12T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "About",
      "order": 6,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "HeLa cells on an electron microscopy grid, imaged twice: an overview of the whole section at 34 nm per pixel, then electron tomograms of single cells at 1.6 nm. The overview is read in place from EMBL's S3 (MoBIE clem-example-project). On the left, each mark is where a tomogram was acquired; zoom in and it becomes the tomogram's footprint. Click one and the right tile opens that tomogram, with Z moving through its depth. Three of the six tomograms are converted for the detail view (binned to 6.2 nm, 18 central slices); the others only mark where they were taken. The tomograms are generated locally by dev/bioimage/make_hela_tomograms.py.\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
